<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1984</h1><p class="ref-lede">1984 in world history: 15 events, 7 deaths and 4 works. 197 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1980">1980</a><a href="/years/1981">1981</a><a href="/years/1982">1982</a><a href="/years/1983">1983</a><a href="/years/1984" aria-current="page">1984</a><a href="/years/1985">1985</a><a href="/years/1986">1986</a><a href="/years/1987">1987</a><a href="/years/1988">1988</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Brunei becomes fully independent from Britain</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The oil-rich sultanate of Brunei ended nearly a century as a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> and became a sovereign state under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hassanal-bolkiah">Hassanal Bolkiah</a>. It joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/association-of-southeast-asian-nations">ASEAN</a> within the week.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-10">10 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">United States and the Holy See establish full diplomatic relations</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">President Reagan's administration and the Vatican agreed to exchange ambassadors, ending a gap in formal relations since 1867. The move reflected close cooperation with Pope John Paul II during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-24">24 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Apple Macintosh goes on sale</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Apple's Macintosh brought the mouse and graphical interface to an affordable personal computer. Launched with a famous television advert, it shaped the design of computers for decades.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-7">7 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Bruce McCandless makes the first untethered spacewalk</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Using a nitrogen-jet backpack, the Manned Maneuvering Unit, McCandless flew about 100 metres from the shuttle Challenger. The photograph of him alone above Earth became famous.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/moscow" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moscow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-6">6 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Alexey Pajitnov completes the first version of Tetris</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Working at a Soviet Academy of Sciences computing centre in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, Pajitnov finished his falling-block puzzle game. It became one of the best-selling video games in history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-25">25 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Svetlana Savitskaya becomes the first woman to walk in space</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet cosmonaut Svetlana Savitskaya spent three and a half hours outside the Salyut 7 space station. She tested a hand-held tool for cutting and welding metal in space.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/golden-temple" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/golden-temple.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-31">31 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Indira Gandhi is assassinated by her bodyguards</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> bodyguards shot Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indira-gandhi">Indira Gandhi</a> in her <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> garden, months after she ordered the army into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-temple">Golden Temple</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a>. Anti-Sikh violence that followed killed about 3,000 people.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-temple">Golden Temple</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amritsar">Amritsar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-3">3 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Toxic gas leaks from a pesticide plant in Bhopal</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Methyl isocyanate escaped from a Union Carbide plant in Bhopal overnight, killing thousands within days. Total deaths are estimated in the range of 15,000 or more, and hundreds of thousands suffered lasting harm.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/operation-blue-star">Operation Blue Star</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Operation Blue Star was the Indian Army's assault in June 1984 on the Golden Temple complex at Amritsar, the holiest shrine of Sikhism, to remove the armed Sikh militant leader Jarnail Singh Bhindranwale and his followers.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/sino-british-joint-declaration" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sino-british-joint-declaration.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/sino-british-joint-declaration">Sino-British Joint Declaration</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Sino-British Joint Declaration was signed in Beijing on 19 December 1984 by Margaret Thatcher and Zhao Ziyang.</p></div></li></ol></section>
